    "q-108048": {
      "dom_id": "step-q108048",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "${(\\frac{1}{16})}^{1}=\\frac{1}{16}$ can be expressed as",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${(\\frac{1}{16})}^{1}=\\frac{1}{16}$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=\\frac{1}{16},b=\\frac{1}{16}$ and $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the equation ${(\\frac{1}{16})}^{1}=\\frac{1}{16}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{1/16}⁡(\\frac{1}{16})=1.$\n\nNote that ${log}_{n}⁡n=1$ for any $n>0,n\\ne 1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
