    "q-99475": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99475",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$\\sqrt{81}=9$ can be expressed as",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the given equation can be written using exponents as follows:\n\n$$\n{81}^{1/2}=9\n$$\n\nThe logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${81}^{1/2}=9$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=9,b=81$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the equation $\\sqrt{81}=9$ is equivalent to ${log}_{81}⁡9=\\frac{1}{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
