    "q-66569": {
      "dom_id": "step-q66569",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$\\sqrt[3]{4}≈1.587$ is equivalent to",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the given approximation can be written using exponents as follows:\n\n$$\n{4}^{1/3}≈1.587\n$$\n\nThe logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${4}^{1/3}≈1.587$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=1.587,b=4$ and $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the approximation $\\sqrt[3]{4}≈1.587$ is equivalent to ${log}_{4}⁡(1.587)≈\\frac{1}{3}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
